{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
AudioMuse-AI (native CPU sidecar) installed.

Quickstart (details: docs/freebsd/26-audiomuse-ai.org in the homelab repo):

1. PostgreSQL: create role+db (or point to an existing cluster):
   psql -c "CREATE ROLE audiomuse LOGIN PASSWORD '...';" \
       -c 'CREATE DATABASE audiomuse OWNER audiomuse;'
2. Edit %%PREFIX%%/etc/audiomuse.env (cp from audiomuse.env.sample):
   set POSTGRES_PASSWORD and Navidrome credentials.
3. Fetch the pinned model set (~5 GB, needs devel/gh):
   doas %%PREFIX%%/bin/audiomuse-setup-models
4. sysrc audiomuse_enable=YES && service audiomuse start
   sysrc audiomuse_worker_enable=YES && service audiomuse_worker start
5. UI: http://127.0.0.1:8000 (setup wizard on first visit).

Models land in /var/db/audiomuse/model (release pins v5.0.0-model / v1 / v1).
EOM
}
